// error
// #4631: `bit check` accepted a READ of a foreign class's unexported field,
// contradicting SPEC §10.5 ("an unexported field is module-private") and the
// grammar at §17.3. `resolveStructFields` (checkbind.bit) unwrapped the
// `export[field[...]]` node and threw the flag away, so no consumer of
// `ctx.structFields` had a visibility bit to consult — the field resolved,
// typed, and lowered like any other. A WRITE was accepted for the same
// reason, and so was a foreign class literal naming the field.
//
// `std/uuid`'s `UUID.hi` is the case the ticket names: `docs/stdlib/uuid.md`
// says "Its fields are private; obtain one from a generator, `parse`, or a
// well-known constructor", and the module's own `version()`/`variant()`
// accessors exist precisely so a caller never needs the raw halves.
//
// Fixed in validatemember.bit's `vForeignFieldAccess`, which `vMember`,
// `vInstMember` (validateinst.bit) and `vCompositeSlot` (validatezero.bit)
// all call, so a read, an instantiated read and a literal slot report the
// same E0046 the resolver already reports for a bad named import.
//
// The second read is #4638. `uuidV4().hi` is the shape #4631's ticket asked
// for, and it exited 0 while the bound form above reported: `vMember` judges
// nothing whose receiver fails `vDeclRooted`, and a call's callee ident is not
// decl-rooted (`declTypes` is written for let/const/param/receiver, never for a
// function), so the chain walk to the base ident answered false. `vChainRooted`
// (validatemember.bit) now accepts a call of a named function declaration, so
// both spellings of the same read are judged. Both are pinned here because a
// guard that skips the receiver and a rule that skips the field are different
// faults with the same symptom -- silence -- and only one line of this file
// would move if either came back.
//
// The third read is #4647. `uuid.uuidV4().hi` exited 0 with #4638 in, because
// a NAMESPACE-qualified call spells its callee as a Member node, which
// `vCalleeIsFuncDecl` answered false for; the walk then reached the base ident
// `uuid`, an `ImportNamespace` with no `declTypes` entry, and the receiver was
// skipped. `vNsCalleeIsFuncDecl` (validatemember.bit) now accepts that callee
// when the base names a namespace import NODE-KEYED through the resolver and
// the dotted name resolves to an exported function declaration. Both imports of
// `std/uuid` are deliberate: one module, both spellings of one call, so the
// three receiver shapes of a single read are pinned against one another.
import { uuidV4 } from "std/uuid"
import uuid from "std/uuid"

fn main() {
  let u = uuidV4()
  println("${u.hi}")
  println("${uuidV4().hi}")
  println("${uuid.uuidV4().hi}")
}
